$ ============================================================== POINT MASSES
$ 19 CONM2s carrying powerplant, systems, furnishing and payload.  Together
$ with ~349 kg of CBAR structural mass the baseline aircraft is 1081 kg with
$ the CG at 22% MAC (x = 2.3934) — 31 points of static margin against a
$ neutral point near 53% MAC, i.e. a conventionally stable GA airplane.
$
$ THIS IS A LUMPED STICK IDEALISATION.  GRID 1 is the engine-mount station
$ and its 313 kg stands for the whole powerplant installation (engine,
$ propeller, spinner, cowling, nose gear, firewall accessories) — ~29% of
$ the aircraft mass on the nose, which is what puts the CG at 22% MAC on
$ this airframe.  The MASSSET cases below move the payload, not this group.
$
$ Fuselage
CONM2, 1, 1, 0, 312.8
CONM2, 2, 900, 0, 203.6
CONM2, 3, 2, 0, 45.0
