CONM2, 6012, 111, 0, 80.0
CONM2, 6013, 12, 0, 40.0
CONM2, 6014, 112, 0, 40.0
$ Full cabin (MASSSET 30 MTOW) — four occupants + baggage, REPLACING the
$ 85 kg baseline card 7.  This one carries an OFFSET: its CG sits 0.35 m aft
$ of and 0.10 m below GRID 2, so the deck exercises the CONM2 offset path
$ (translation-rotation coupling and the parallel-axis transfer) inside a
$ mass case rather than only at the baseline.
CONM2, 6020, 2, 0, 324.0, 0.35, 0.0, -0.10
$
$ ============================================================== MASS CASES
$ Three payload conditions over one airframe.  Stiffness, splines and the
$ whole VLM AeroCache are geometry/Mach-only and are built ONCE and shared;
$ only M_gg, M_ax, GPWG and the trim solve are rebuilt per case.
$
$   MASSSET 10  FERRY    996.0 kg   baseline less the rear-seat payload
$   MASSSET 20  CRUISE  1201.0 kg   baseline + 120 kg half wing fuel
$   MASSSET 30  MTOW    1560.0 kg   baseline + 240 kg full wing fuel
$                                   + rear-seat payload 85 -> 324 kg
$
$ The bare deck (no MASSSET selected) is the 1081.0 kg baseline.  All three
$ ops are exercised: DELETE by 10, ADD by 20 and 30, REPLACE by 30.
$
$ Physics the sweep demonstrates: heavier cases must trim to a larger ANGLEA
$ at the same q, AND the wing-root bending per unit aircraft weight must FALL
$ as fuel goes into the wing — inertia relief, because wing fuel is carried
$ outboard of the root cut and its weight cancels part of the lift there.
MASSSET, 10, FERRY, 1.0
+, DELETE, 7
MASSSET, 20, CRUISE, 1.0
+, ADD, 6001, 6002, 6003, 6004
MASSSET, 30, MTOW, 1.0
+, ADD, 6011, 6012, 6013, 6014
+, REPLACE, 7, 6020
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------- CONSTRAINTS
$ Full-span free-flight support, NOT a ground mount.  Pin the four non-trim
$ rigid-body modes (Tx, Ty, Rx, Rz) at the single reference point GRID 900;
$ SUPORT carries the two symmetric trim DOFs (Tz, Ry).  Under symmetric loads
$ the antisymmetric DOFs come out ~0 with no SPC needed, so the airframe
$ deforms freely and both wings react through the fuselage.
SPC1, 1, 1246, 900
SUPORT, 900, 35
$
$ ============================================================== AERODYNAMICS
$ Reference geometry (full-span): CREF = wing MAC, BREF = wing span,
$ SREF = wing area.  RCSID = 990 puts the rigid-body motion and the reported
$ moments in the z-down stability axis at the quarter-MAC.
$ Field 8 (sbeam extension) is the default Mach for Prandtl-Glauert.
AEROS, 0, 990, 1.4707, 11.20, 16.24, 0, 0, 0.0
$
$ Aerodynamic panel property
PAERO1, 10
$
$ MESH SIZING.  NCHORD = 6 chordwise on every surface: >= 2 is required for
$ the section-moment correction at all, and >= 4 is needed before the
$ pitching moment converges; 6 leaves margin at the 2.5g operating point.
$ NSPAN is then chosen per surface to keep the box aspect ratio near 1, which
$ is what the VLM's horseshoe-vortex kernel is best conditioned for.
$ CAERO1 EIDs are 1000-spaced so every box ID (EID + i_span*NCHORD + j_chord)
$ stays inside its own decade: 1000-1095, 2000-2095, 3000-3047, 4000-4047,
$ 5000-5035.  6000/7000 are RESERVED for the Step 66 body panels.
$
$ ---- Wing starboard: 16 x 6 = 96 boxes (1000-1095)
CAERO1, 1000, 10, 0, 16, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 2.00, 0.0, 1.250, 1.75, 2.15, 5.60, 1.397, 1.15
$ ---- Wing port: 16 x 6 = 96 boxes (2000-2095)
CAERO1, 2000, 10, 0, 16, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 2.00, 0.0, 1.250, 1.75, 2.15, -5.60, 1.397, 1.15
$
$ ---- HTP starboard: 8 x 6 = 48 boxes (3000-3047)
CAERO1, 3000, 10, 0, 8, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 6.90, 0.0, 0.70, 1.05, 7.10, 1.73, 0.70, 0.75
$ ---- HTP port: 8 x 6 = 48 boxes (4000-4047)
CAERO1, 4000, 10, 0, 8, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 6.90, 0.0, 0.70, 1.05, 7.10, -1.73, 0.70, 0.75
$
$ ---- VTP (single surface, "span" is Z): 6 x 6 = 36 boxes (5000-5035)
CAERO1, 5000, 10, 0, 6, 6, 0, 0, 1
+, 6.60, 0.0, 0.80, 1.50, 7.10, 0.0, 2.30, 0.85
$
$ ================================================================== SPLINES
$ Four SPLINE2 beam splines (wing L/R, HTP L/R) plus one ATTACH (fin).
$
$ DTHY MUST BE 0.0 ON EVERY SPLINE2 HERE.  Each SET1 lists elastic-axis grids
$ only, and those are collinear along the spline axis, so the beam spline has
$ NO twist information of its own: detaching torsion (DTHY = -1, the HA144A
$ setting, which works there because its SET1s carry LE/TE stringer PAIRS)
$ leaves the spline system singular and the operator build raises ValueError.
$ DTHY = 0.0 attaches torsion rigidly to the EA rotation, which is exactly
$ right for a stick model whose only twist DOF is the beam's own Rx/Ry.
$ DTHX is left at its 0.0 default for the same reason.
$
$ ---- RIGHT wing: boxes 1000-1095 to the starboard EA, axis CID 991
SET1, 1010, 10, 11, 12
SPLINE2, 1001, 1000, 1000, 1095, 1010, 0.0, 1.0, 991
$ ---- LEFT wing: boxes 2000-2095 to the port EA, axis CID 992
SET1, 1020, 10, 111, 112
SPLINE2, 1002, 2000, 2000, 2095, 1020, 0.0, 1.0, 992
$ ---- RIGHT HTP: boxes 3000-3047 to the starboard HTP EA, axis CID 993
SET1, 1030, 20, 21, 22
SPLINE2, 1003, 3000, 3000, 3047, 1030, 0.0, 1.0, 993
$ ---- LEFT HTP: boxes 4000-4047 to the port HTP EA, axis CID 994
SET1, 1040, 20, 121, 122
SPLINE2, 1004, 4000, 4000, 4047, 1040, 0.0, 1.0, 994
$
$ ---- VTP: ATTACH, not SPLINE2.
$ The fin is short, stiff and vertical.  Two reasons it gets the rigid
$ attachment instead of a beam spline: (a) a SPLINE2 would need a spline-axis
$ CORD2R whose y-axis runs along global Z, the awkward case; (b) the fin's
$ own bending is negligible next to the tailcone bending that carries it, so
$ rigidly slaving all 36 fin boxes to the fin-root grid is the physically
$ honest idealisation.  ATTACH requires CID = 0.
ATTACH, 1005, 5000, 5000, 5035, 30, 0
$
$ ============================================================ MONITOR POINTS
$ Integrated section loads for the structures/loads handoff.  Two flavours:
$   MONPNT1 = AERO ONLY, summed over a box collection (AELIST);
$   MONPNT3 = AERO + INERTIA + REACTION, summed over structural grids (SET1).
$ On a balanced maneuver the whole-aircraft MONPNT1 returns n*W while the
$ whole-aircraft MONPNT3 returns ~0 — that contrast is the point of having
$ both, and it is the cheapest end-to-end check that the trim really balanced.
$
$ ---- Right wing outboard of the root cut.
$ Deliberately EXCLUDES the shared root grid 10: taken about the root station
$ (2.70, 0, 1.25), the resultant of grids 11 and 12 IS the starboard
$ wing-root shear and bending moment.
SET1, 1300, 11, 12
AECOMP, RWINGEA, SET1, 1300
MONPNT3, MWROOT, RIGHT WING ROOT, 35, RWINGEA, 0, 2.70, 0.0, 1.25
$
$ ---- Whole aircraft.
$ DEF-M10 RULE: this SET1 must list EVERY spline-load grid AND EVERY
$ CONM2-bearing grid.  Grids 1, 900, 3, 5, 31 and 32 carry mass but take no
$ spline load; leaving any of them out silently drops that share of the
$ inertia and the "MONPNT3 ~ 0" balance check stops meaning anything.
$ Overlay (MASSSET) CONM2s live on grids 2, 11, 12, 111, 112 — already here.
SET1, 1310, 1, 900, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 11
+, 12, 111, 112, 20, 21, 22, 121, 122
+, 30, 31, 32
AECOMP, ALLGRID, SET1, 1310
MONPNT3, MALLEA, WHOLE AIRCRAFT, 35, ALLGRID, 0, 2.4375, 0.0, 0.60
$
$ ---- Whole-aircraft aero, and starboard-wing aero (aero-only).
AELIST, 1400, 1000, THRU, 1095, 2000, THRU, 2095, 3000, THRU, 3047
+, 4000, THRU, 4047, 5000, THRU, 5035
AECOMP, ALLAERO, AELIST, 1400
MONPNT1, MALLAR, AIRCRAFT AERO, 35, ALLAERO, 0, 2.4375, 0.0, 0.60
AELIST, 1410, 1000, THRU, 1095
AECOMP, RWAERO, AELIST, 1410
MONPNT1, MRWAER, RIGHT WING AERO, 35, RWAERO, 0, 2.70, 0.0, 1.25
$
$ ---- Section-cut running loads (MONSECT, Monitor Phase 2).
$ Where a MONPNT3 gives ONE resultant, a MONSECT sweeps the same sum over a
$ list of cut planes and returns the per-station {shear, bending, torque} table
$ the stress group sizes the wing from.
$ CID 991 is the right wing's SPLINE2 axis, reused verbatim as the cut frame:
$ its y-axis is the elastic axis, so the default AXIS=2 measures stations along
$ the EA and every cut's moment reference lands on it.  Stations are chosen
$ clear of the EA grids (11 at 2.801, 12 at 5.603) so no cut lands on a grid;
$ 6.50 is outboard of the tip and must return exactly zero.
$ Under a MASSSET case the wing-fuel CONM2s on grids 11/12 enter the inertia
$ column automatically, so the table is per mass case with no extra cards.
MONSECT, SECRW, RIGHT WING LOADS, RWINGEA, 991
+, 0.30, 1.50, 4.20, 6.50
$ The same stations taken aero-only (an AELIST-type AECOMP), for the airload
$ distribution without the inertia relief.
MONSECT, SECRWA, RIGHT WING AIRLOAD, RWAERO, 991
+, 0.30, 1.50, 4.20, 6.50
